        "Content": "Kellyville is a charming and significant country house extending to 2500 Sq Ft of luxurious accommodation in pristine condition set on a beautiful elevated and mature site in an area of exceptional natural beauty and close to all amenities. A magnificent late Victorian country house with complete refurbishment and an exceptional extension, this breathtakingly beautiful home is a rare gem.\n\nApproached by a gated entrance with attractive wing walls and twin pillars, this picture postcard residence oozes kerb appeal with its part stone façade, slate roof and traditional gables. Drive along the crunch gravel entrance and you will immediately appreciate a home abundant in period style yet offering levels of modern comforts and rarely found in a house with this charm.\n\nThe ground floor is beautifully presented and stunningly detailed in an elegant country-house style, combining warmth and character with generous proportions and an impeccable standard of condition throughout.\n\nA welcoming entrance hallway with timber flooring and a striking traditional staircase immediately sets the tone for the home. \n\nAt the heart of the home is the impressive country-style kitchen, extending to almost 6 metres in length. Rich timber cabinetry, traditional detailing and excellent worktop space give the room tremendous character, while the large window draws in an abundance of natural light and enjoys a lovely outlook over the gardens. There is ample space for family dining. There is a separate and spacious utility room and a guest WC adding excellent practicality.\n\nThe dining room is just off the kitchen and is a particularly attractive, light-filled reception room, beautifully finished and opening through French doors to the outside, creating a wonderful setting for both family dining and entertaining.\n\nThe superb living room is flooded with natural light, with two sets of glazed doors framing the gardens and creating a wonderful connection between the house and its surroundings. Timber flooring and a traditional solid-fuel stove further enhance its relaxed country-house atmosphere.\n\nCompleting the ground floor is a substantial home office, beautifully detailed with a handsome period-style fireplace and extensive fitted shelving. Generous enough to serve equally well as a library, study, playroom or additional reception room, it adds considerable versatility to the accommodation.\n\nAdding to the home?s authentic country charm are two separate staircases, a delightful feature entirely in keeping with its traditional period character.\n\nImpeccably maintained, beautifully proportioned and presented with exceptional attention to detail, the entire ground floor has a wonderfully refined country-house feel while remaining warm, comfortable and entirely suited to modern family living.\n\nThe first floor continues the home?s wonderfully distinctive country-house character, with a superb sense of space, warmth and craftsmanship throughout. Four generously proportioned bedrooms are arranged around two landings, with beautiful natural timber floors, extensive timber-panelled ceilings and traditional ledged-and-braced doors creating a particularly attractive and cohesive finish.\n\nThe bedrooms are exceptionally spacious, enjoying impressive vaulted ceilings that add both scale and architectural interest. Deep-set windows, a rooflight and plentiful natural light complement the rich timber detailing, while the tasteful country-style presentation gives the accommodation a relaxed and welcoming feel.\n\nThere are two bathrooms at this level, including a particularly charming bathroom with a freestanding roll-top bath, separate shower and striking patterned floor. A second shower room provides excellent additional facilities for family or guests.\n\nImpeccably presented throughout, this is an unusually spacious and beautifully detailed upper floor, perfectly complementing the exceptional country-house style of the accommodation below.\n\nThe exterior perfectly complements the beautifully presented interior, with the property enjoying a wonderfully private country-house setting surrounded by mature gardens and open countryside.\n\nThe house itself has enormous character, combining an attractive natural stone façade with traditional white-rendered elevations and a slate roof. A large mature weeping willow forms a magnificent centrepiece to the front, giving the property an immediately established and distinctive appearance.\n\nThe residence is approached through a walled and gated entrance, opening onto an exceptionally generous gravelled forecourt providing extensive parking and turning space. A detached garage which is superbly appointed as a workshop sits neatly to one side, while attractive stone paving extends across the front of the house.\n\nTo the rear lies a superb expanse of mature, beautifully maintained lawn, bordered by established hedging and trees and enjoying wonderful privacy. An established small orchard adds greatly to the country-house atmosphere, with productive apple trees and walnut trees framing delightful views back towards the residence. The gardens have a wonderfully relaxed character, with ample space for outdoor entertaining, children's play or simply enjoying the peaceful rural surroundings.\n\nA particularly charming feature is the property's kitchen-garden character, complete with a polytunnel/greenhouse and additional garden structures, while the orchard and roaming hens create an idyllic sense of country living.\n\nBeyond the gardens, the property enjoys an attractive open aspect across adjoining farmland, reinforcing the feeling of space and tranquillity.\n\nOverall, the grounds are exceptionally generous, mature and beautifully established, offering the privacy and atmosphere of a genuine country home while remaining practical, manageable and superbly presented.\n\nBallintubbert house & gardens and St Josephs Gaa are just a stone?s through away. Primary and Secondary schools are nearby and with the towns of Stradbally, Carlow and Athy all close by, everything is at hand.\n\nViewing Of This Beautiful Home Is Highly Recommended\n"
